.TH XPS13-CAMERA-CHROME-FIX 1 "November 2026" "xps13-ubuntu-camera 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
xps13-camera-chrome-fix \- allow Google Chrome to use the camera through the desktop portal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xps13-camera-chrome-fix
.RB [ yes | no ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
With Chrome's PipeWire camera support enabled, the unsandboxed Chrome asks the
xdg-desktop-portal for camera access, but GNOME refuses to show the access dialog and the
request is denied, so video calls (e.g. Google Meet) hang. This stores the answer for
Chrome's app IDs (google-chrome, com.google.Chrome) in the user's portal permission store,
as clicking "Allow" would. Run as the desktop user, then restart Chrome.
Websites still ask for camera permission inside Chrome.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xps13-camera-check (1)
